From 9202aa4ffce7a8d8ed07cd0b3f324a6aff23983e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bemly <bemly_@petalmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 15:33:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Sinytra patch 0013: resource://android resolves to provider
 APK

In a System-WebView provider context, getApplicationContext() returns
the host app's context, so getPackageResourcePath() would return the
host APK path. This breaks resource://android/assets/... URIs (used by
the internal sinytra-js WebExtension): nsResProtocolHandler::GetApkURI
calls GeckoAppShell::getPackageResourcePath via JNI, constructs
jar:file://<host-apk>!/..., and file-not-found kills the extension load.

Symptom: PostMessage 8 fail + console/beforeunload/Geo-accept failures
in CTS (pid 20099 logcat shows 'Error while loading manifest.json
(NS_ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND)').

Solution: Use the same classloader-derived provider APK resolution as
GeckoThread.getOmnijarApk (patch 0008). Regular embedders unaffected:
their classloader resolves to the context APK, fallback returns it.
---
 .../java/org/mozilla/gecko/GeckoAppShell.java | 29 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/gecko/GeckoAppShell.java b/mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/gecko/GeckoAppShell.java
index be91e2d312e8..17e44131b0e6 100644
--- a/mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/gecko/GeckoAppShell.java
+++ b/mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/gecko/GeckoAppShell.java
@@ -1457,9 +1457,36 @@ public class GeckoAppShell {
     }
   }
 
+  // Sinytra patch 0013 (2026-10-01): resource://android must resolve to the
+  // provider APK, not the host APK. This is the C++ side of the resource protocol
+  // (nsResProtocolHandler::GetApkURI calls this via JNI). In a System-WebView
+  // provider context, getApplicationContext() returns the host app's context,
+  // so resource://android/assets/sinytra-js/manifest.json would resolve to
+  // jar:file://<host-apk>!/assets/sinytra-js/manifest.json (which does not exist).
+  // The internal WebExtension then fails to load, killing eval/postMessage/console.
+  // Use the same classloader-derived logic as GeckoThread.getOmnijarApk (0008).
   @WrapForJNI
   public static String getPackageResourcePath() {
-    return getApplicationContext().getPackageResourcePath();
+    final Context context = getApplicationContext();
+    final String resourcePath = context.getPackageResourcePath();
+    try {
+      final String mozglue =
+          ((dalvik.system.BaseDexClassLoader) GeckoAppShell.class.getClassLoader())
+              .findLibrary("mozglue");
+      if (mozglue != null) {
+        final int apkSplit = mozglue.lastIndexOf("!/");
+        if (apkSplit > 0) {
+          final String apk = mozglue.substring(0, apkSplit);
+          if (!apk.equals(resourcePath)) {
+            Log.w(LOGTAG, "resource://android: using provider apk " + apk);
+            return apk;
+          }
+        }
+      }
+    } catch (final Throwable t) {
+      Log.w(LOGTAG, "resource://android: context apk fallback", t);
+    }
+    return resourcePath;
   }
 
   @WrapForJNI(calledFrom = "any")
-- 
2.56.0

